    "faq_question_answer_BG3KbA": {
      "type": "faq-question-answer",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_XGtxB7": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "faq_que": "How to Stop Braided Sleeving From Fraying?",
            "faq_ans": "<p>When terminating braided sleeving, use a hot knife to keep the ends from fraying. Once the sleeving is cut, use pliers, or an inverted funnel to flare the ends to allow the sleeving to slide easily over your application. <a href=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0892/0583/4033/files/How_To_Cut_Sleeving_Using_A_Hot_Knife.pdf?v=1743592295\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0892/0583/4033/files/How_To_Cut_Sleeving_Using_A_Hot_Knife.pdf?v=1743592295\"><strong>...more</strong></a></p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_CfDGWa": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "faq_que": "How to Use Expandable Braided Sleeving?",
            "faq_ans": "<p>When covering A/V, electrical, industrial, etc. wires and cables, expandable sleeving can be used. Some PET sleeves expand up to four times the sleeve's original diameter. <a href=\"/blogs/how-to/how-to-use-braided-sleeving-in-diy-wire-cable-management-projects\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"How to Use Braided Sleeving In DIY Wire & Cable Management Projects\"><strong>...more</strong></a></p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_DUHT8B": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "faq_que": "What Size Braided Sleeving Should I Use?",
            "faq_ans": "<p>First, determine the diameter of the bundle of cables that you will be covering with braided sleeving. For snug fittings, try using expandable rigid sleeves and wraps; these allow for a range of fitting options. Or you can select a smaller braided sleeving with a diameter that is slightly smaller than your bundle of cables. For a loose fit, use a sleeve that is the same or slightly larger than your bundled cables. <a href=\"/blogs/how-to/how-to-determine-which-product-diameter-you-need\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"How to Determine Which Product Diameter You Need\"><strong>...more</strong></a></p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_KmTiit": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "faq_que": "When Should I Use Braided Sleeving?",
            "faq_ans": "<p>People use braided sleeving for full coverage protection of their cables. There are many braided sleeving solutions for the automotive, military, and even aerospace industries. Braided sleeving, like PET Wrap, can be used for at home cable management. <a href=\"/blogs/articles/cable-management-tips-resources\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Cable Management Tips & Resources\"><strong>...more</strong></a></p><p>Braided Sleeving is used not only for bundling longer cables, but can also be used to help protect your wires and cables from chemicals, heat, and other environmental factors. <a href=\"/blogs/how-to/how-to-use-braided-sleeving-in-diy-wire-cable-management-projects\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"How to Use Braided Sleeving In DIY Wire & Cable Management Projects\"><strong>...more</strong></a></p><p>Certain sleeving products like metal braided sleeving can be used for things like wildlife installations due to it's mesh-like features. <a href=\"/blogs/articles/protecting-your-pets-with-corrugated-wire-loom-tubing\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Protecting Your Pets with Corrugated Wire Loom Tubing\"><strong>...more</strong></a></p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "faq_XGtxB7",
        "faq_CfDGWa",
        "faq_DUHT8B",
        "faq_KmTiit"
      ],
      "settings": {
        "button_text": "go back FAQ landing page",
        "button_link": "shopify://pages/faq",
        "faq_heading": "Braided Sleeving"
      }
    },
    "faq_question_answer_EbdUeD": {
      "type": "faq-question-answer",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_G8jM9G": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "faq_que": "How to Use Wire Loom Insertion Tool",
            "faq_ans": "<p>First, gather your cables together and insert the bundle through the wire loom installation tool. Next, start sliding the tool through the wire loom until you reach the end. Lastly remove the tool and you have successfully managed your cables! <a href=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0892/0583/4033/files/wireloom-install-instructions.pdf?v=1748891551\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0892/0583/4033/files/wireloom-install-instructions.pdf?v=1748891551\"><strong>...more</strong></a></p><p>Once your cables have been bundled and insterted in the tool, place the bulge of the tool under the end of the split tubing. Slide along the length of the tubing until you reach the end. Rotate the barrel and remove the tool from the bundled cables. Smooth out the sleeving with your hand and trim the excess wire loom. <a href=\"/blogs/how-to/how-to-tame-cables-with-wire-loom\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"How to Tame Cables with Wire Loom\"><strong>...more</strong></a></p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_jHVQca": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "faq_que": "What is Wire Loom Used For?",
            "faq_ans": "<p>Wire Loom is used for tidying up cables. The split down the side of this tubing allows for easy addition and removal of cables. People with pets and children choose wire loom to prevent wires from being chewed on/ damaged. <a href=\"/blogs/how-to/how-to-keep-your-cables-tidy\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"How to Keep Your Cables Tidy\"><strong>...more</strong></a></p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_hFUerz": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "faq_que": "What Size Wire Loom Do I Need?",
            "faq_ans": "<p>Gather together your cables that you want to bundle together. Measure the diameter of this bundle and select a wire loom with a diameter of equal or greater value. <a href=\"/blogs/how-to/how-to-determine-which-product-diameter-you-need\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"How to Determine Which Product Diameter You Need\"><strong>...more</strong></a></p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "faq_G8jM9G",
        "faq_jHVQca",
        "faq_hFUerz"
      ],
      "settings": {
        "button_text": "",
        "button_link": "",
        "faq_heading": "Wire Loom"
      }
    },
    "faq_question_answer_nDGPTP": {
      "type": "faq-question-answer",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_xRW4pk": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "faq_que": "What is the Purpose of Cable Tray?",
            "faq_ans": "<p>Cable trays are the perfect solution when you need to run high quantities of power and data cables. These cable trays provide support and a route for your cables. <a href=\"/blogs/articles/cable-management-tips-resources\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Cable Management Tips & Resources\"><strong>...more</strong></a></p><p>Cable trays are a great way to get your cables off of the floor. Cable baskets are a great option for desk wire management — these trays simply attach to the underside of your desk and allow cables to break out wherever needed. <a href=\"/blogs/articles/desk-cable-organizers\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Desk Cable Organizers\"><strong>...more</strong></a></p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_CMpKNg": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "faq_que": "Where Can I Use Cable Trays?",
            "faq_ans": "<p>Cable trays can be used under your floors or in the ceiling. <a href=\"/blogs/articles/cable-management-tips-resources\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Cable Management Tips & Resources\"><strong>...more</strong></a></p><p>Cable basket trays can be used in places like offices by simply attaching the basket underneath a desk. <a href=\"/blogs/articles/desk-cable-organizers\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Desk Cable Organizers\"><strong>...more</strong></a></p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "faq_xRW4pk",
        "faq_CMpKNg"
      ],
      "settings": {
        "button_text": "",
        "button_link": "",
        "faq_heading": "Cable Tray Systems"
      }
    },
